      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Highways do serve suburban and rural communities but need to be balanced with other infrastructure investments. Focusing solely on highways could lead to congestion and sprawl, negatively impacting overall mobility. By investing in public transit, cities can provide affordable and sustainable options for suburban and rural residents to access city centers without relying on cars, thus creating a more equitable transportation network and reducing environmental impact over the long term. Balancing road maintenance with improvements in public transit ensures that all areas benefit holistically, both in terms of transportation and quality of life.",
      "source": "target",
